C o m p i l a t i o n


   1  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
   2  SETS cars  car produced /Coup, Minivan/
   3       res resources /Metal, Circuit, Labor/;
   4   
   5  * 2. DEFINE input data
   6  PARAMETERS
   7     c(cars) Objective function coefficients ($ per plant)
   8           /Coup 6000,
   9           Minivan 7000 /
  10   
  11     b(res) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  12            /Metal 4000000,
  13             Circuit  12000,
  14             Labor  17500/;
  15   
  16  TABLE A(cars,res) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  17                   Metal    Circuit  Labor
  18   Coup           1000      4        5
  19   Minivan        2000      3        2.5;
  20   
  21   
  22  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  23  VARIABLES X(cars) cars produced (Number)
  24            VPROFIT  total profit ($);
  25   
  26  * Non-negativity constraints
  27  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  28   
  29  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  30  EQUATIONS
  31     PROFIT Total profit ($) and objective function value
  32     RES_CONSTRAIN(res) Resource Constraints;
  33   
  34  PROFIT..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(cars, c(cars)*X(cars));
  35  RES_CONSTRAIN(res) ..    SUM(cars, A(cars,res)*X(cars)) =L= b(res);
  36   
  37   
  38  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  39  MODEL PRODUCTION /PROFIT, RES_CONSTRAIN/;
  40  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  41  *MODEL PLANTING /ALL/;
  42   
  43   
  44  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  45  * Solve the PLANTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  46  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  47  SOLVE PRODUCTION USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  48   
  49   
  50  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


